<article class="env-lemma" id="054N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/054N">Lemma <span data-tag="054N">33.7.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme over the field $k$. Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. Then $X$ is geometrically connected over $k$ if and only if $X_{k'}$ is geometrically connected over $k'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $X$ is geometrically connected over $k$, then it is clear that $X_{k'}$ is geometrically connected over $k'$. For the converse, for any field extension $k''/k$ there exists a common field extension $k'''/k'$ and $k'''/k''$, see Fields, Lemma <a href="/tag/0H7K" data-tag="0H7K">9.6.9</a>. As the morphism $X_{k'''} \to X_{k''}$ is surjective (as a base change of a surjective morphism between spectra of fields) we see that the connectedness of $X_{k'''}$ implies the connectedness of $X_{k''}$. Thus if $X_{k'}$ is geometrically connected over $k'$ then $X$ is geometrically connected over $k$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>